        "evidence": "Most of this proof checks out exactly; one braid word does not, and it contradicts the block's own next paragraph. VERIFIED CORRECT, all recomputed at 30 dps against an independently built 2-dimensional H_3(q) representation: the Hoefsmit entries alpha = -1/(q^3+q) and gamma = q^3/(q^2+1) satisfy alpha + gamma = h and alpha*gamma = -1/([3]+1) to 32 digits, exactly as claimed; the arithmetic -alpha*gamma(1+[3]) - ([3]-1) = 1 - [3] + 1 = 2 - [3] is right; tr(T_1 T_2^-1) = 2 - [3]_q = -1.043706209; the Chebyshev step tr(M^3) = t^3 - 3t is right and gives 1.99418581298 at the proton pin, matching the block's \"approximately 1.994\" and the corpus's independent closed form 2 - 3h^4 - h^6; [2]_q^2 = 4.043706209, matching \"approximately 4.04\"; and the precision floor delta_q = 1.4e-9 reproduces - differentiating m_mu/m_e = Vol(4_1)/hbar_q^2 gives dR/dq = -3387.6, and CODATA's 22 ppb on the ratio gives delta_q = 1.343e-9. WRONG: \"4_1 = T_1 T_2^-1 T_1^-1 T_2 is the commutator [T_1, T_2^-1]\". That word's closure is the UNKNOT - I computed its Alexander polynomial from the reduced Burau representation and got 1, against t - 3 + t^-1 for (T_1 T_2^-1)^2, which is the figure-eight. The block contradicts itself two paragraphs later, where the Borromean argument calls T_1 T_2^-1 \"the first factor of 4_1\" - true only if 4_1 = (T_1 T_2^-1)^2, which is what the rest of the corpus says. So the figure-eight computation is a correct computation of the wrong word, and its result propagates into the statement block's table.",
